Precipitate insoluble in nitric acid confirms BaSO4 (sulfate). 

The cation is K+ (pale violet flame). The solution is strongly acidic (pH=2). For a pure K salt of sulfate, K2SO4 would be neutral (pH~7). The acidic pH=2 indicates the anion is HSO4-, so the salt is KHSO4 (potassium hydrogen sulfate / potassium bisulfate).

Final Answer: {"cation": "K+", "anion": "HSO4-"}
